{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J7gRDWtkhprrsLd1HJwhYD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/internal.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! quic-core's grand internal header.  Anything that is not\n4\t//! part of the published `quic.h` API but is shared between\n5\t//! `.c` files of the core library lives here: connection /\n6\t//! path / stream / packet structures, frame and packet-type\n7\t//! enums, the giant `Quic` and `Connection`\n8\t//! structures that pin the rest of the library together, and\n9\t//! the long internal-only function surface (~200 functions).\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every function body is\n12\t//! `todo!()`.  Test module at the end is intentionally empty;\n13\t//! Phase 2 fills it.\n14\t//!\n15\t//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n16\t//!\n17\t//! * Single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields collapse to\n18\t//!   `bool` per field (the \"ordinary integer field with\n19\t//!   mask/shift accessors\" rule, simplified for the trivial\n20\t//!   1-bit case where `bool` is clearer than `u32` + masks).\n21\t//! * Phase 1B replaced the C intrusive linked-list / splay /\n22\t//!   hash linkage with arena tokens\n23\t//!   ([`crate::arena::Token`], [`crate::splay::SplayToken`],\n24\t//!   [`crate::hash::HashToken`]).  Every per-collection\n25\t//!   membership is `Option<Token>` on the parent struct; the\n26\t//!   container holds the slot storage.  Zero raw pointers, no\n27\t//!   `unsafe`.\n28\t//! * The C `void* tls_master_ctx`, `void* aead_*`,\n29\t//!   `void* pn_enc/dec`, etc. were external-library handles\n30\t//!   ((picotls, OpenSSL).  Phase 2 replaced them with the\n31\t//!   trait family in [`crate::tls`] (`Session`, `PacketKey`,\n32\t//!   `HeaderKey`, …); backends supply implementations.\n33\t//! * `FILE* F_log` / `FILE* f_binlog` became\n34\t//!   `Option<std::fs::File>` in Phase 1B.\n35\t//! * `struct sockaddr_storage` fields fold into\n36\t//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  Fields that the C code zeros out\n37\t//!   to mean \"address not yet set\" become `Option<SocketAddr>`.\n38\t//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` were\n39\t//!   forward-declared as opaque stubs in\n40\t//!   [`crate`] (the public header).  Their\n41\t//!   real bodies live here; the public module re-exports the\n42\t//!   names so existing `use` paths in other modules keep\n43\t//!   working.\n44\t//! * Function pointer typedefs (`autoqlog_fn`,\n45\t//!   `performance_log_fn`, the spin-bit pair, the\n46\t//!   memlog hook on a connection, `mask_fns_t`) collapse to\n47\t//!   traits per the project rule.  When two function pointers\n48\t//!   are always installed together (`SpinbitDef`,\n49\t//!   `mask_fns_t`) they share one trait.\n50\t//! * Conditional fields gated by `BBRExperiment` and\n51\t//!   `WITH_THREAD_CHECK` are dropped — they are not\n52\t//!   part of the v1 target build.\n53\t//! * The `PARSE_*`/`IS_*_STREAM_ID(_*)` macros that the C\n54\t//!   header inlines as preprocessor macros are translated to\n55\t//!   `pub const fn` helpers.\n56\t\n57\tuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\n58\tuse std::fs::File;\n59\tuse std::path::PathBuf;\n60\t\n61\tuse core::any::Any;\n62\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n63\t\n64\tuse crate::arena::{Arena, Token};\n65\tuse crate::hash::{HashTable, HashToken};\n66\tuse crate::splay::{SplayToken, SplayTree};\n67\tuse crate::{Duration, Instant};\n68\t\n69\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` connection arena.\n70\t///\n71\t/// Phase 4 plan: every C `*mut picoquic_cnx_t` becomes a\n72\t/// [`ConnectionToken`].  Following it requires `quic.connections.get(tok)`\n73\t/// — one indirection through the arena, plus a generation check.\n74\t/// Stable across operations on other connections.\n75\tpub type ConnectionToken = Token<Connection>;\n76\t\n77\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` registered-token replay-protection arena.\n78\tpub type RegisteredTokenToken = Token<RegisteredToken>;\n79\t\n80\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` issued-tickets arena (server-side replay state).\n81\tpub type IssuedTicketToken = Token<IssuedTicket>;\n82\t\n83\t/// Token into the per-`Connection` (or per-`StreamHead`) stream-related\n84\t/// arenas.  Phase 4 may further split these into per-collection types.\n85\tpub type StreamToken = Token<StreamHead>;\n86\tpub type StreamDataToken = Token<StreamDataNode>;\n87\tpub type PacketToken = Token<Packet>;\n88\tpub type SackItemToken = Token<SackItem>;\n89\tpub type LocalConnectionIdToken = Token<LocalConnectionId>;\n90\tpub type PathToken = Token<Path>;\n91\tuse crate::logger::Logger;\n92\tuse crate::{\n93\t    AlpnSelect, CongestionAlgorithm, ConnectionId, ConnectionIdCallback, Fuzz, LossbitVersion,\n94\t    PacketContext, PathStatus, PmtudPolicy, RESET_SECRET_SIZE, SpinbitVersion, State,\n95\t    StreamDataCallback, StreamDirectReceive, TransportParameters,\n96\t};\n97\t\n98\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n99\t// Tunable constants (the `#define`s at the top of the C header).\n100\t\n101\tpub const MAX_PACKET_SIZE: usize = 1536;\n102\tpub const MIN_SEGMENT_SIZE: usize = 256;\n103\tpub const ENFORCED_INITIAL_MTU: usize = 1200;\n104\tpub const ENFORCED_INITIAL_CID_LENGTH: u8 = 8;\n105\tpub const PRACTICAL_MAX_MTU: usize = 1440;\n106\tpub const MIN_STREAM_DATA_FRAGMENT: usize = 512;\n107\tpub const RETRY_SECRET_SIZE: usize = 64;\n108\tpub const RETRY_TOKEN_PAD_SIZE: usize = 26;\n109\tpub const DEFAULT_0RTT_WINDOW: usize = 10 * ENFORCED_INITIAL_MTU;\n110\tpub const NB_PATH_TARGET: usize = 8;\n111\tpub const NB_PATH_DEFAULT: usize = 2;\n112\tpub const MAX_PACKETS_IN_POOL: i32 = 0x2000;\n113\tpub const INITIAL_FLOW_CONTROL_MAX: u64 = 0x100000;\n114\t\n115\tpub const INITIAL_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(250_000);\n116\tpub const TARGET_RENO_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(100_000);\n117\tpub const TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(610_000);\n118\tpub const INITIAL_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(250_000);\n119\tpub const INITIAL_MAX_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000_000);\n120\tpub const LARGE_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(2_000_000);\n121\tpub const MIN_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(50_000);\n122\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000);\n123\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MAX_DEFAULT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(25_000);\n124\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MIN: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000);\n125\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MIN_MAX_VALUE: u64 = 0xFFFFFF;\n126\tpub const RACK_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000);\n127\tpub const MAX_ACK_DELAY_MAX_MS: u64 = 0x4000;\n128\tpub const TOKEN_DELAY_LONG: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(24 * 60 * 60 * 1_000_000);\n129\tpub const TOKEN_DELAY_SHORT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(2 * 60 * 1_000_000);\n130\tpub const CID_REFRESH_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(5 * 1_000_000);\n131\tpub const MTU_LOSS_THRESHOLD: u64 = 10;\n132\t\n133\tpub const BANDWIDTH_ESTIMATE_MAX: u64 = 10_000_000_000;\n134\tpub const BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MIN: u64 = 1000;\n135\tpub const BANDWIDTH_MEDIUM: u64 = 2_000_000;\n136\tpub const MAX_BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MIN: u64 = 1000;\n137\tpub const MAX_BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MAX: u64 = 15000;\n138\t\n139\tpub const MINRTT_MARGIN: u64 = 128;\n140\tpub const MINRTT_THRESHOLD: u64 = 128;\n141\t\n142\tpub const SPURIOUS_RETRANSMIT_DELAY_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000_000);\n143\t\n144\tpub const MICROSEC_SILENCE_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(120_000_000);\n145\tpub const MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(30_000_000);\n146\tpub const MICROSEC_WAIT_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000_000);\n147\t\n148\tpub const MICROSEC_STATELESS_RESET_INTERVAL_DEFAULT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(100_000);\n149\t\n150\tpub const CWIN_INITIAL: u64 = 10 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;\n151\tpub const CWIN_MINIMUM: u64 = 2 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;\n152\t\n153\tpub const DEFAULT_CRYPTO_EPOCH_LENGTH: u64 = 1 << 22;\n154\t\n155\tpub const DEFAULT_SIMULTANEOUS_LOGS: u32 = 32;\n156\tpub const DEFAULT_HALF_OPEN_RETRY_THRESHOLD: u32 = 64;\n157\t\n158\tpub const PN_RANDOM_MIN: u32 = 0xffff;\n159\tpub const PN_RANDOM_RANGE: u32 = 0x10000;\n160\t\n161\tpub const SPIN_RESERVE_MOD_256: u8 = 17;\n162\t\n163\tpub const CHALLENGE_REPEAT_MAX: usize = 3;\n164\t\n165\tpub const ALPN_NUMBER_MAX: usize = 32;\n166\t\n167\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_NEW_RENO: u8 = 1;\n168\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_CUBIC: u8 = 2;\n169\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_DCUBIC: u8 = 3;\n170\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_FAST: u8 = 4;\n171\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_BBR: u8 = 5;\n172\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_PRAGUE: u8 = 6;\n173\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_BBR1: u8 = 7;\n174\t\n175\tpub const MAX_ACK_RANGE_REPEAT: usize = 4;\n176\tpub const MIN_ACK_RANGE_REPEAT: usize = 2;\n177\t\n178\tpub const DEFAULT_HOLE_PERIOD: u64 = 256;\n179\t\n180\tpub const LOSS_BIT_Q_HALF_PERIOD: u64 = 64;\n181\t\n182\tpub const NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS: usize = 4;\n183\tpub const NUMBER_OF_EPOCH_OFFSETS: usize = NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS + 1;\n184\t\n185\tpub use crate::tp::NB_TP_0RTT;\n186\t\n187\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n188\t// Range / bitfield helper macros.\n189\t\n190\t/// `IN_RANGE(v, min, max)` — true when `min ≤ v ≤ max`\n191\t/// under the C macro's bitfield assumption (`min & max == min`,\n192\t/// `min & bits == 0`, `max & bits == bits`).\n193\t#[inline]\n194\tpub const fn in_range(v: u64, min: u64, max: u64) -> bool {\n195\t    (v & !(min ^ max)) == min\n196\t}\n197\t\n198\t/// `BITS_SET_IN_RANGE(v, min, max, bits)`.\n199\t#[inline]\n200\tpub const fn bits_set_in_range(v: u64, min: u64, max: u64, bits: u64) -> bool {\n201\t    (v & !(min ^ max ^ bits)) == (min ^ bits)\n202\t}\n203\t\n204\t/// `BITS_CLEAR_IN_RANGE(v, min, max, bits)`.\n205\t#[inline]\n206\tpub const fn bits_clear_in_range(v: u64, min: u64, max: u64, bits: u64) -> bool {\n207\t    (v & !(min ^ max ^ bits)) == min\n208\t}\n209\t\n210\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n211\t// Frame types.\n212\t\n213\t// `FrameType` lives in [`crate::frames`].\n214\t\n215\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n216\t// PMTU discovery requirement status.\n217\t\n218\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\n219\t#[repr(u8)]\n220\tpub enum PmtuDiscoveryStatus {\n221\t    #[default]\n222\t    NotNeeded = 0,\n223\t    Optional,\n224\t    Required,\n225\t}\n226\t\n227\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n228\t// Supported QUIC versions.\n229\t\n230\t/// QUIC version codes recognised by this build.  Wire values are the\n231\t/// `u32` `Initial` packet version field; `TryFrom<u32>` converts an\n232\t/// arbitrary wire value to a [`Version`] (or fails when the version\n233\t/// isn't recognised).\n234\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n235\t#[repr(u32)]\n236\tpub enum Version {\n237\t    SeventeenthInterop = 0xFF00001B,\n238\t    EighteenthInterop = 0xFF00001C,\n239\t    NineteenthInterop = 0xFF00001D,\n240\t    NineteenthBisInterop = 0xFF00001E,\n241\t    TwentiethPreInterop = 0xFF00001F,\n242\t    TwentiethInterop = 0xFF000020,\n243\t    TwentyFirstInterop = 0xFF000021,\n244\t    PostIesg = 0xFF000022,\n245\t    V1 = 0x00000001,\n246\t    V2 = 0x6b3343cf,\n247\t    V2Draft = 0x709a50c4,\n248\t    InternalTest1 = 0x50435130,\n249\t    InternalTest2 = 0x50435131,\n250\t}\n251\t\n252\t/// First entry in `Version`'s declaration order — the canonical\n253\t/// interop version reported by `INTEROP_VERSION_LATEST` in C.\n254\tpub const INTEROP_VERSION_LATEST: Version = Version::NineteenthInterop;\n255\t\n256\timpl Version {\n257\t    /// Resolve `proposed` to a known [`Version`] (RFC 9000 §15\n258\t    /// \"Versions\").  C: `get_version_index`.\n259\t    pub fn try_from_wire(proposed: u32) -> Option<Self> {\n260\t        // SKIP: try_from_wire: version table requires static crypto byte arrays not yet wired up;\n261\t        // returning None for all until Version::parameters is implemented\n262\t        match proposed {\n263\t            0x00000001 => Some(Version::V1),\n264\t            0x6b3343cf => Some(Version::V2),\n265\t            0x709a50c4 => Some(Version::V2Draft),\n266\t            0xFF00001B => Some(Version::SeventeenthInterop),\n267\t            0xFF00001C => Some(Version::EighteenthInterop),\n268\t            0xFF00001D => Some(Version::NineteenthInterop),\n269\t            0xFF00001E => Some(Version::NineteenthBisInterop),\n270\t            0xFF00001F => Some(Version::TwentiethPreInterop),\n271\t            0xFF000020 => Some(Version::TwentiethInterop),\n272\t            0xFF000021 => Some(Version::TwentyFirstInterop),\n273\t            0xFF000022 => Some(Version::PostIesg),\n274\t            0x50435130 => Some(Version::InternalTest1),\n275\t            0x50435131 => Some(Version::InternalTest2),\n276\t            _ => None,\n277\t        }\n278\t    }\n279\t\n280\t    /// Per-version cryptographic and label parameters.  C:\n281\t    /// `picoquic_supported_versions[]`'s row for this version.\n282\t    pub fn parameters(self) -> VersionParameters {\n283\t        // SKIP: parameters: requires static crypto byte slices from C tables not yet ported\n284\t        // Returning a placeholder V1 parameters for now\n285\t        VersionParameters {\n286\t            version: self,\n287\t            version_aead_key: &[],\n288\t            version_retry_key: &[],\n289\t            tls_prefix_label: \"tls13 quic \",\n290\t            tls_traffic_update_label: \"quic ku\",\n291\t            packet_type_version: self as u32,\n292\t            upgrade_from: &[],\n293\t        }\n294\t    }\n295\t}\n296\t\n297\t/// Per-version cryptographic and label parameters.  C:\n298\t/// `VersionParameters`.\n299\t///\n300\t/// `version_aead_key` and `version_retry_key` are static byte\n301\t/// tables in the C source — Rust models them as borrowed slices.\n302\t/// `upgrade_from` is a `NULL`-terminated list in C; here it is a\n303\t/// borrowed slice, with an empty slice for \"no upgrade path\".\n304\t#[derive(Debug)]\n305\tpub struct VersionParameters {\n306\t    pub version: Version,\n307\t    pub version_aead_key: &'static [u8],\n308\t    pub version_retry_key: &'static [u8],\n309\t    pub tls_prefix_label: &'static str,\n310\t    pub tls_traffic_update_label: &'static str,\n311\t    pub packet_type_version: u32,\n312\t    pub upgrade_from: &'static [Version],\n313\t}\n314\t\n315\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n316\t// Crypto epochs and packet types.\n317\t\n318\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n319\t#[repr(u8)]\n320\tpub enum Epoch {\n321\t    Initial = 0,\n322\t    ZeroRtt = 1,\n323\t    Handshake = 2,\n324\t    OneRtt = 3,\n325\t}\n326\t\n327\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n328\t#[repr(u8)]\n329\tpub enum PacketType {\n330\t    Error = 0,\n331\t    VersionNegotiation,\n332\t    Initial,\n333\t    Retry,\n334\t    Handshake,\n335\t    ZeroRttProtected,\n336\t    OneRttProtected,\n337\t    TypeMax,\n338\t}\n339\t\n340\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n341\t// Packet header.\n342\t\n343\t/// Parsed long/short packet header.  C: `PacketHeader`.\n344\t///\n345\t/// The C struct uses a packed bitfield for eight single-bit\n346\t/// flags; Rust stores them as plain `bool` fields (one per flag).\n347\tpub struct PacketHeader {\n348\t    pub dest_connection_id: ConnectionId,\n349\t    pub src_connection_id: ConnectionId,\n350\t    /// Truncated packet number as it appeared on the wire (1-4 bytes,\n351\t    /// extended to `u32`).  Reconstructed full PN is in\n352\t    /// [`Self::packet_number_full`].\n353\t    pub packet_number_truncated: u32,\n354\t    pub version: u32,\n355\t    pub offset: usize,\n356\t    pub packet_number_offset: usize,\n357\t    pub packet_type: PacketType,\n358\t    pub packet_number_mask: u64,\n359\t    pub packet_number_full: u64,\n360\t    pub payload_length: usize,\n361\t    pub version_index: i32,\n362\t    pub epoch: Epoch,\n363\t    pub packet_context: PacketContext,\n364\t\n365\t    pub key_phase: bool,\n366\t    pub spin: bool,\n367\t    pub has_spin_bit: bool,\n368\t    pub has_reserved_bit_set: bool,\n369\t    pub has_loss_bits: bool,\n370\t    pub loss_bit_q: bool,\n371\t    pub loss_bit_l: bool,\n372\t    pub quic_bit_is_zero: bool,\n373\t\n374\t    /// Borrowed token bytes (length implicit in the slice).  Phase\n375\t    /// 4 plan: `IncomingPacket` decoders carry a lifetime; the\n376\t    /// `token_length` field is gone (it lived only as the slice's\n377\t    /// length).\n378\t    pub token_bytes: Vec<u8>,\n379\t    pub payload_length_value: usize,\n380\t    /// Token into [`Quic`]'s arena for the local CID this packet\n381\t    /// targets, if any.  C: `*mut LocalConnectionId` back-pointer.\n382\t    pub local_connection_id: Option<LocalConnectionIdToken>,\n383\t}\n384\t\n385\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n386\t// Spin-bit policy vtable.\n387\t\n388\t/// Spin-bit policy: how to update the spin bit on an incoming\n389\t/// packet, and what value to emit on outgoing packets.  In C the\n390\t/// policy is two function pointers grouped into\n391\t/// `SpinbitDef`; the two are always installed\n392\t/// together so they share one Rust trait.\n393\tpub trait SpinBitPolicy: Sync {\n394\t    /// C: `spinbit_incoming_fn`.\n395\t    fn incoming(&self, connection: &mut Connection, path_x: &mut Path, ph: &PacketHeader);\n396\t\n397\t    /// C: `spinbit_outgoing_fn`.\n398\t    fn outgoing(&self, connection: &mut Connection) -> u8;\n399\t}\n400\t\n401\t/// Spin-bit policy dispatch table.  Replaces `extern SpinbitDef\n402\t/// spin_function_table[]` from the C source.  Each row is a\n403\t/// `&'static dyn` to a stateless policy implementor; the wrapper\n404\t/// `SpinbitDef` struct from C is gone (the trait object carries\n405\t/// the same information).\n406\t///\n407\t/// Indices match [`crate::SpinbitVersion`] values:\n408\t/// * 0 = Basic\n409\t/// * 1 = Random\n410\t/// * 2 = Null\n411\t/// * 3 = On (test-only, server side)\n412\t///\n413\t/// The concrete policy types and the populated table land in\n414\t/// `crate::spinbit` (Phase 4).\n415\tpub static SPIN_FUNCTION_TABLE: &[&dyn SpinBitPolicy] = &[];\n416\t\n417\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n418\t// Stateless packet, queued at the QUIC context until sendable.\n419\t\n420\tpub struct StatelessPacket {\n421\t    pub addr_to: SocketAddr,\n422\t    pub addr_local: SocketAddr,\n423\t    pub if_index_local: i32,\n424\t    pub received_ecn: u8,\n425\t    pub length: usize,\n426\t    pub receive_time: Instant,\n427\t    pub connection_id_log64: u64,\n428\t    pub initial_connection_id: ConnectionId,\n429\t    pub packet_type: PacketType,\n430\t    pub bytes: [u8; MAX_PACKET_SIZE],\n431\t}\n432\t\n433\timpl Quic {\n434\t    /// Allocate a fresh stateless-packet buffer.  C:\n435\t    /// `create_stateless_packet` plus the per-context pool;\n436\t    /// `Quic.connections.alloc()`-style — Rust uses normal heap\n437\t    /// allocation and lets `Drop` free.\n438\t    pub fn create_stateless_packet(&mut self) -> Result<StatelessPacket, crate::Error> {\n439\t        use core::net::{IpAddr, Ipv4Addr};\n440\t        Ok(StatelessPacket {\n441\t            addr_to: core::net::SocketAddr::new(IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::UNSPECIFIED), 0),\n442\t            addr_local: core::net::SocketAddr::new(IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::UNSPECIFIED), 0),\n443\t            if_index_local: 0,\n444\t            received_ecn: 0,\n445\t            length: 0,\n446\t            receive_time: crate::Instant::from_ticks(0),\n447\t            connection_id_log64: 0,\n448\t            initial_connection_id: crate::ConnectionId::default(),\n449\t            packet_type: crate::internal::PacketType::Error,\n450\t            bytes: [0u8; crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE],\n451\t        })\n452\t    }\n453\t\n454\t    /// Hand `sp` to the QUIC context's pending stateless-packet\n455\t    /// queue.  C: `queue_stateless_packet`.\n456\t    pub fn queue_stateless_packet(&mut self, sp: StatelessPacket) {\n457\t        self.pending_stateless_packets.push_back(sp);\n458\t    }\n459\t\n460\t    /// Pop the next pending stateless packet.  Returns `None` when\n461\t    /// the queue is empty.  C: `dequeue_stateless_packet`.\n462\t    pub fn dequeue_stateless_packet(&mut self) -> Option<StatelessPacket> {\n463\t        self.pending_stateless_packets.pop_front()\n464\t    }\n465\t}\n466\t\n467\t// `delete_stateless_packet` is gone -- StatelessPacket falls out\n468\t// of scope (the VecDeque drains it); `Drop` does the C `free`.\n469\t\n470\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n471\t// Stream data nodes (received) and queue nodes (queued for send).\n472\t\n473\tpub struct StreamDataNode {\n474\t    /// Membership in the parent stream's `stream_data_tree`.\n475\t    /// `Some(token)` while in the tree; `None` otherwise.  Phase 4\n476\t    /// uses this for O(1) removal.\n477\t    pub stream_data_membership: Option<SplayToken>,\n478\t    pub offset: u64,\n479\t    /// Inline buffer of payload bytes.  C kept a parallel\n480\t    /// `bytes: *const u8` aliasing into `data` plus a `length`\n481\t    /// field; in Rust the slice subsumes both — `data[..len]` is\n482\t    /// the live payload and `len` is `length`.\n483\t    pub data: [u8; MAX_PACKET_SIZE],\n484\t    pub length: usize,\n485\t}\n486\t\n487\tpub struct StreamQueueNode {\n488\t    pub offset: u64,\n489\t    /// Owned send-queue payload.  C: `bytes: *mut u8` plus paired\n490\t    /// `length: size_t`; both collapse into the vector.\n491\t    pub bytes: Vec<u8>,\n492\t}\n493\t\n494\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n495\t// Sent packet (kept on retransmit queues until acked).\n496\t\n497\tpub struct Packet {\n498\t    /// Membership in the owning connection's\n499\t    /// `queue_data_repeat_tree`.  Phase 4 uses this for O(1) removal.\n500\t    pub queue_data_repeat_membership: Option<SplayToken>,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e30a456-15c0-4e3c-af27-9f4dab375915","uuid":"5d552b72-83ad-4126-bbef-0189818f3c29","timestamp":"2026-05-05T21:18:41.830Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/internal.rs","content":"//! Translation of `quic/internal.h`.\n//!\n//! quic-core's grand internal header.  Anything that is not\n//! part of the published `quic.h` API but is shared between\n//! `.c` files of the core library lives here: connection /\n//! path / stream / packet structures, frame and packet-type\n//! enums, the giant `Quic` and `Connection`\n//! structures that pin the rest of the library together, and\n//! the long internal-only function surface (~200 functions).\n//!\n//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every function body is\n//! `todo!()`.  Test module at the end is intentionally empty;\n//! Phase 2 fills it.\n//!\n//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n//!\n//! * Single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields collapse to\n//!   `bool` per field (the \"ordinary integer field with\n//!   mask/shift accessors\" rule, simplified for the trivial\n//!   1-bit case where `bool` is clearer than `u32` + masks).\n//! * Phase 1B replaced the C intrusive linked-list / splay /\n//!   hash linkage with arena tokens\n//!   ([`crate::arena::Token`], [`crate::splay::SplayToken`],\n//!   [`crate::hash::HashToken`]).  Every per-collection\n//!   membership is `Option<Token>` on the parent struct; the\n//!   container holds the slot storage.  Zero raw pointers, no\n//!   `unsafe`.\n//! * The C `void* tls_master_ctx`, `void* aead_*`,\n//!   `void* pn_enc/dec`, etc. were external-library handles\n//!   ((picotls, OpenSSL).  Phase 2 replaced them with the\n//!   trait family in [`crate::tls`] (`Session`, `PacketKey`,\n//!   `HeaderKey`, …); backends supply implementations.\n//! * `FILE* F_log` / `FILE* f_binlog` became\n//!   `Option<std::fs::File>` in Phase 1B.\n//! * `struct sockaddr_storage` fields fold into\n//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  Fields that the C code zeros out\n//!   to mean \"address not yet set\" become `Option<SocketAddr>`.\n//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` were\n//!   forward-declared as opaque stubs in\n//!   [`crate`] (the public header).  Their\n//!   real bodies live here; the public module re-exports the\n//!   names so existing `use` paths in other modules keep\n//!   working.\n//! * Function pointer typedefs (`autoqlog_fn`,\n//!   `performance_log_fn`, the spin-bit pair, the\n//!   memlog hook on a connection, `mask_fns_t`) collapse to\n//!   traits per the project rule.  When two function pointers\n//!   are always installed together (`SpinbitDef`,\n//!   `mask_fns_t`) they share one trait.\n//! * Conditional fields gated by `BBRExperiment` and\n//!   `WITH_THREAD_CHECK` are dropped — they are not\n//!   part of the v1 target build.\n//! * The `PARSE_*`/`IS_*_STREAM_ID(_*)` macros that the C\n//!   header inlines as preprocessor macros are translated to\n//!   `pub const fn` helpers.\n\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\nuse std::fs::File;\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\n\nuse core::any::Any;\nuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n\nuse crate::arena::{Arena, Token};\nuse crate::hash::{HashTable, HashToken};\nuse crate::splay::{SplayToken, SplayTree};\nuse crate::{Duration, Instant};\n\n/// Token into the per-`Quic` connection arena.\n///\n/// Phase 4 plan: every C `*mut picoquic_cnx_t` becomes a\n/// [`ConnectionToken`].  Following it requires `quic.connections.get(tok)`\n/// — one indirection through the arena, plus a generation check.\n/// Stable across operations on other connections.\npub type ConnectionToken = Token<Connection>;\n\n/// Token into the per-`Quic` registered-token replay-protection arena.\npub type RegisteredTokenToken = Token<RegisteredToken>;\n\n/// Token into the per-`Quic` issued-tickets arena (server-side replay state).\npub type IssuedTicketToken = Token<IssuedTicket>;\n\n/// Token into the per-`Connection` (or per-`StreamHead`) stream-related\n/// arenas.  Phase 4 may further split these into per-collection types.\npub type StreamToken = Token<StreamHead>;\npub type StreamDataToken = Token<StreamDataNode>;\npub type PacketToken = Token<Packet>;\npub type SackItemToken = Token<SackItem>;\npub type LocalConnectionIdToken = Token<LocalConnectionId>;\npub type PathToken = Token<Path>;\nuse crate::logger::Logger;\nuse crate::{\n    AlpnSelect, CongestionAlgorithm, ConnectionId, ConnectionIdCallback, Fuzz, LossbitVersion,\n    PacketContext, PathStatus, PmtudPolicy, RESET_SECRET_SIZE, SpinbitVersion, State,\n    StreamDataCallback, StreamDirectReceive, TransportParameters,\n};\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Tunable constants (the `#define`s at the top of the C header).\n\npub const MAX_PACKET_SIZE: usize = 1536;\npub const MIN_SEGMENT_SIZE: usize = 256;\npub const ENFORCED_INITIAL_MTU: usize = 1200;\npub const ENFORCED_INITIAL_CID_LENGTH: u8 = 8;\npub const PRACTICAL_MAX_MTU: usize = 1440;\npub const MIN_STREAM_DATA_FRAGMENT: usize = 512;\npub const RETRY_SECRET_SIZE: usize = 64;\npub const RETRY_TOKEN_PAD_SIZE: usize = 26;\npub const DEFAULT_0RTT_WINDOW: usize = 10 * ENFORCED_INITIAL_MTU;\npub const NB_PATH_TARGET: usize = 8;\npub const NB_PATH_DEFAULT: usize = 2;\npub const MAX_PACKETS_IN_POOL: i32 = 0x2000;\npub const INITIAL_FLOW_CONTROL_MAX: u64 = 0x100000;\n\npub const INITIAL_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(250_000);\npub const TARGET_RENO_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(100_000);\npub const TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(610_000);\npub const INITIAL_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(250_000);\npub const INITIAL_MAX_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000_000);\npub const LARGE_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(2_000_000);\npub const MIN_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(50_000);\npub const ACK_DELAY_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000);\npub const ACK_DELAY_MAX_DEFAULT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(25_000);\npub const ACK_DELAY_MIN: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000);\npub const ACK_DELAY_MIN_MAX_VALUE: u64 = 0xFFFFFF;\npub const RACK_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000);\npub const MAX_ACK_DELAY_MAX_MS: u64 = 0x4000;\npub const TOKEN_DELAY_LONG: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(24 * 60 * 60 * 1_000_000);\npub const TOKEN_DELAY_SHORT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(2 * 60 * 1_000_000);\npub const CID_REFRESH_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(5 * 1_000_000);\npub const MTU_LOSS_THRESHOLD: u64 = 10;\n\npub const BANDWIDTH_ESTIMATE_MAX: u64 = 10_000_000_000;\npub const BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MIN: u64 = 1000;\npub const BANDWIDTH_MEDIUM: u64 = 2_000_000;\npub const MAX_BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MIN: u64 = 1000;\npub const MAX_BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MAX: u64 = 15000;\n\npub const MINRTT_MARGIN: u64 = 128;\npub const MINRTT_THRESHOLD: u64 = 128;\n\npub const SPURIOUS_RETRANSMIT_DELAY_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000_000);\n\npub const MICROSEC_SILENCE_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(120_000_000);\npub const MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(30_000_000);\npub const MICROSEC_WAIT_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000_000);\n\npub const MICROSEC_STATELESS_RESET_INTERVAL_DEFAULT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(100_000);\n\npub const CWIN_INITIAL: u64 = 10 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;\npub const CWIN_MINIMUM: u64 = 2 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;\n\npub const DEFAULT_CRYPTO_EPOCH_LENGTH: u64 = 1 << 22;\n\npub const DEFAULT_SIMULTANEOUS_LOGS: u32 = 32;\npub const DEFAULT_HALF_OPEN_RETRY_THRESHOLD: u32 = 64;\n\npub const PN_RANDOM_MIN: u32 = 0xffff;\npub const PN_RANDOM_RANGE: u32 = 0x10000;\n\npub const SPIN_RESERVE_MOD_256: u8 = 17;\n\npub const CHALLENGE_REPEAT_MAX: usize = 3;\n\npub const ALPN_NUMBER_MAX: usize = 32;\n\npub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_NEW_RENO: u8 = 1;\npub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_CUBIC: u8 = 2;\npub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_DCUBIC: u8 = 3;\npub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_FAST: u8 = 4;\npub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_BBR: u8 = 5;\npub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_PRAGUE: u8 = 6;\npub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_BBR1: u8 = 7;\n\npub const MAX_ACK_RANGE_REPEAT: usize = 4;\npub const MIN_ACK_RANGE_REPEAT: usize = 2;\n\npub const DEFAULT_HOLE_PERIOD: u64 = 256;\n\npub const LOSS_BIT_Q_HALF_PERIOD: u64 = 64;\n\npub const NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS: usize = 4;\npub const NUMBER_OF_EPOCH_OFFSETS: usize = NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS + 1;\n\npub use crate::tp::NB_TP_0RTT;\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Range / bitfield helper macros.\n\n/// `IN_RANGE(v, min, max)` — true when `min ≤ v ≤ max`\n/// under the C macro's bitfield assumption (`min & max == min`,\n/// `min & bits == 0`, `max & bits == bits`).\n#[inline]\npub const fn in_range(v: u64, min: u64, max: u64) -> bool {\n    (v & !(min ^ max)) == min\n}\n\n/// `BITS_SET_IN_RANGE(v, min, max, bits)`.\n#[inline]\npub const fn bits_set_in_range(v: u64, min: u64, max: u64, bits: u64) -> bool {\n    (v & !(min ^ max ^ bits)) == (min ^ bits)\n}\n\n/// `BITS_CLEAR_IN_RANGE(v, min, max, bits)`.\n#[inline]\npub const fn bits_clear_in_range(v: u64, min: u64, max: u64, bits: u64) -> bool {\n    (v & !(min ^ max ^ bits)) == min\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Frame types.\n\n// `FrameType` lives in [`crate::frames`].\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// PMTU discovery requirement status.\n\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\n#[repr(u8)]\npub enum PmtuDiscoveryStatus {\n    #[default]\n    NotNeeded = 0,\n    Optional,\n    Required,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Supported QUIC versions.\n\n/// QUIC version codes recognised by this build.  Wire values are the\n/// `u32` `Initial` packet version field; `TryFrom<u32>` converts an\n/// arbitrary wire value to a [`Version`] (or fails when the version\n/// isn't recognised).\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n#[repr(u32)]\npub enum Version {\n    SeventeenthInterop = 0xFF00001B,\n    EighteenthInterop = 0xFF00001C,\n    NineteenthInterop = 0xFF00001D,\n    NineteenthBisInterop = 0xFF00001E,\n    TwentiethPreInterop = 0xFF00001F,\n    TwentiethInterop = 0xFF000020,\n    TwentyFirstInterop = 0xFF000021,\n    PostIesg = 0xFF000022,\n    V1 = 0x00000001,\n    V2 = 0x6b3343cf,\n    V2Draft = 0x709a50c4,\n    InternalTest1 = 0x50435130,\n    InternalTest2 = 0x50435131,\n}\n\n/// First entry in `Version`'s declaration order — the canonical\n/// interop version reported by `INTEROP_VERSION_LATEST` in C.\npub const INTEROP_VERSION_LATEST: Version = Version::NineteenthInterop;\n\nimpl Version {\n    /// Resolve `proposed` to a known [`Version`] (RFC 9000 §15\n    /// \"Versions\").  C: `get_version_index`.\n    pub fn try_from_wire(proposed: u32) -> Option<Self> {\n        // SKIP: try_from_wire: version table requires static crypto byte arrays not yet wired up;\n        // returning None for all until Version::parameters is implemented\n        match proposed {\n            0x00000001 => Some(Version::V1),\n            0x6b3343cf => Some(Version::V2),\n            0x709a50c4 => Some(Version::V2Draft),\n            0xFF00001B => Some(Version::SeventeenthInterop),\n            0xFF00001C => Some(Version::EighteenthInterop),\n            0xFF00001D => Some(Version::NineteenthInterop),\n            0xFF00001E => Some(Version::NineteenthBisInterop),\n            0xFF00001F => Some(Version::TwentiethPreInterop),\n            0xFF000020 => Some(Version::TwentiethInterop),\n            0xFF000021 => Some(Version::TwentyFirstInterop),\n            0xFF000022 => Some(Version::PostIesg),\n            0x50435130 => Some(Version::InternalTest1),\n            0x50435131 => Some(Version::InternalTest2),\n            _ => None,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Per-version cryptographic and label parameters.  C:\n    /// `picoquic_supported_versions[]`'s row for this version.\n    pub fn parameters(self) -> VersionParameters {\n        // SKIP: parameters: requires static crypto byte slices from C tables not yet ported\n        // Returning a placeholder V1 parameters for now\n        VersionParameters {\n            version: self,\n            version_aead_key: &[],\n            version_retry_key: &[],\n            tls_prefix_label: \"tls13 quic \",\n            tls_traffic_update_label: \"quic ku\",\n            packet_type_version: self as u32,\n            upgrade_from: &[],\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Per-version cryptographic and label parameters.  C:\n/// `VersionParameters`.\n///\n/// `version_aead_key` and `version_retry_key` are static byte\n/// tables in the C source — Rust models them as borrowed slices.\n/// `upgrade_from` is a `NULL`-terminated list in C; here it is a\n/// borrowed slice, with an empty slice for \"no upgrade path\".\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct VersionParameters {\n    pub version: Version,\n    pub version_aead_key: &'static [u8],\n    pub version_retry_key: &'static [u8],\n    pub tls_prefix_label: &'static str,\n    pub tls_traffic_update_label: &'static str,\n    pub packet_type_version: u32,\n    pub upgrade_from: &'static [Version],\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Crypto epochs and packet types.\n\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n#[repr(u8)]\npub enum Epoch {\n    Initial = 0,\n    ZeroRtt = 1,\n    Handshake = 2,\n    OneRtt = 3,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n#[repr(u8)]\npub enum PacketType {\n    Error = 0,\n    VersionNegotiation,\n    Initial,\n    Retry,\n    Handshake,\n    ZeroRttProtected,\n    OneRttProtected,\n    TypeMax,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Packet header.\n\n/// Parsed long/short packet header.  C: `PacketHeader`.\n///\n/// The C struct uses a packed bitfield for eight single-bit\n/// flags; Rust stores them as plain `bool` fields (one per flag).\npub struct PacketHeader {\n    pub dest_connection_id: ConnectionId,\n    pub src_connection_id: ConnectionId,\n    /// Truncated packet number as it appeared on the wire (1-4 bytes,\n    /// extended to `u32`).  Reconstructed full PN is in\n    /// [`Self::packet_number_full`].\n    pub packet_number_truncated: u32,\n    pub version: u32,\n    pub offset: usize,\n    pub packet_number_offset: usize,\n    pub packet_type: PacketType,\n    pub packet_number_mask: u64,\n    pub packet_number_full: u64,\n    pub payload_length: usize,\n    pub version_index: i32,\n    pub epoch: Epoch,\n    pub packet_context: PacketContext,\n\n    pub key_phase: bool,\n    pub spin: bool,\n    pub has_spin_bit: bool,\n    pub has_reserved_bit_set: bool,\n    pub has_loss_bits: bool,\n    pub loss_bit_q: bool,\n    pub loss_bit_l: bool,\n    pub quic_bit_is_zero: bool,\n\n    /// Borrowed token bytes (length implicit in the slice).  Phase\n    /// 4 plan: `IncomingPacket` decoders carry a lifetime; the\n    /// `token_length` field is gone (it lived only as the slice's\n    /// length).\n    pub token_bytes: Vec<u8>,\n    pub payload_length_value: usize,\n    /// Token into [`Quic`]'s arena for the local CID this packet\n    /// targets, if any.  C: `*mut LocalConnectionId` back-pointer.\n    pub local_connection_id: Option<LocalConnectionIdToken>,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Spin-bit policy vtable.\n\n/// Spin-bit policy: how to update the spin bit on an incoming\n/// packet, and what value to emit on outgoing packets.  In C the\n/// policy is two function pointers grouped into\n/// `SpinbitDef`; the two are always installed\n/// together so they share one Rust trait.\npub trait SpinBitPolicy: Sync {\n    /// C: `spinbit_incoming_fn`.\n    fn incoming(&self, connection: &mut Connection, path_x: &mut Path, ph: &PacketHeader);\n\n    /// C: `spinbit_outgoing_fn`.\n    fn outgoing(&self, connection: &mut Connection) -> u8;\n}\n\n/// Spin-bit policy dispatch table.  Replaces `extern SpinbitDef\n/// spin_function_table[]` from the C source.  Each row is a\n/// `&'static dyn` to a stateless policy implementor; the wrapper\n/// `SpinbitDef` struct from C is gone (the trait object carries\n/// the same information).\n///\n/// Indices match [`crate::SpinbitVersion`] values:\n/// * 0 = Basic\n/// * 1 = Random\n/// * 2 = Null\n/// * 3 = On (test-only, server side)\n///\n/// The concrete policy types and the populated table land in\n/// `crate::spinbit` (Phase 4).\npub static SPIN_FUNCTION_TABLE: &[&dyn SpinBitPolicy] = &[];\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Stateless packet, queued at the QUIC context until sendable.\n\npub struct StatelessPacket {\n    pub addr_to: SocketAddr,\n    pub addr_local: SocketAddr,\n    pub if_index_local: i32,\n    pub received_ecn: u8,\n    pub length: usize,\n    pub receive_time: Instant,\n    pub connection_id_log64: u64,\n    pub initial_connection_id: ConnectionId,\n    pub packet_type: PacketType,\n    pub bytes: [u8; MAX_PACKET_SIZE],\n}\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Allocate a fresh stateless-packet buffer.  C:\n    /// `create_stateless_packet` plus the per-context pool;\n    /// `Quic.connections.alloc()`-style — Rust uses normal heap\n    /// allocation and lets `Drop` free.\n    pub fn create_stateless_packet(&mut self) -> Result<StatelessPacket, crate::Error> {\n        use core::net::{IpAddr, Ipv4Addr};\n        Ok(StatelessPacket {\n            addr_to: core::net::SocketAddr::new(IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::UNSPECIFIED), 0),\n            addr_local: core::net::SocketAddr::new(IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::UNSPECIFIED), 0),\n            if_index_local: 0,\n            received_ecn: 0,\n            length: 0,\n            receive_time: crate::Instant::from_ticks(0),\n            connection_id_log64: 0,\n            initial_connection_id: crate::ConnectionId::default(),\n            packet_type: crate::internal::PacketType::Error,\n            bytes: [0u8; crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE],\n        })\n    }\n\n    /// Hand `sp` to the QUIC context's pending stateless-packet\n    /// queue.  C: `queue_stateless_packet`.\n    pub fn queue_stateless_packet(&mut self, sp: StatelessPacket) {\n        self.pending_stateless_packets.push_back(sp);\n    }\n\n    /// Pop the next pending stateless packet.  Returns `None` when\n    /// the queue is empty.  C: `dequeue_stateless_packet`.\n    pub fn dequeue_stateless_packet(&mut self) -> Option<StatelessPacket> {\n        self.pending_stateless_packets.pop_front()\n    }\n}\n\n// `delete_stateless_packet` is gone -- StatelessPacket falls out\n// of scope (the VecDeque drains it); `Drop` does the C `free`.\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Stream data nodes (received) and queue nodes (queued for send).\n\npub struct StreamDataNode {\n    /// Membership in the parent stream's `stream_data_tree`.\n    /// `Some(token)` while in the tree; `None` otherwise.  Phase 4\n    /// uses this for O(1) removal.\n    pub stream_data_membership: Option<SplayToken>,\n    pub offset: u64,\n    /// Inline buffer of payload bytes.  C kept a parallel\n    /// `bytes: *const u8` aliasing into `data` plus a `length`\n    /// field; in Rust the slice subsumes both — `data[..len]` is\n    /// the live payload and `len` is `length`.\n    pub data: [u8; MAX_PACKET_SIZE],\n    pub length: usize,\n}\n\npub struct StreamQueueNode {\n    pub offset: u64,\n    /// Owned send-queue payload.  C: `bytes: *mut u8` plus paired\n    /// `length: size_t`; both collapse into the vector.\n    pub bytes: Vec<u8>,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Sent packet (kept on retransmit queues until acked).\n\npub struct Packet {\n    /// Membership in the owning connection's\n    /// `queue_data_repeat_tree`.  Phase 4 uses this for O(1) removal.\n    pub queue_data_repeat_membership: Option<SplayToken>,","numLines":500,"startLine":1,"totalLines":5041}}}
