{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JYRhCRxVE4M2bMeMW8mov8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/internal.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! quic-core's grand internal header.  Anything that is not\n4\t//! part of the published `quic.h` API but is shared between\n5\t//! `.c` files of the core library lives here: connection /\n6\t//! path / stream / packet structures, frame and packet-type\n7\t//! enums, the giant `Quic` and `Connection`\n8\t//! structures that pin the rest of the library together, and\n9\t//! the long internal-only function surface (~200 functions).\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every function body is\n12\t//! `todo!()`.  Test module at the end is intentionally empty;\n13\t//! Phase 2 fills it.\n14\t//!\n15\t//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n16\t//!\n17\t//! * Single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields collapse to\n18\t//!   `bool` per field (the \"ordinary integer field with\n19\t//!   mask/shift accessors\" rule, simplified for the trivial\n20\t//!   1-bit case where `bool` is clearer than `u32` + masks).\n21\t//! * Phase 1B replaced the C intrusive linked-list / splay /\n22\t//!   hash linkage with arena tokens\n23\t//!   ([`crate::arena::Token`], [`crate::splay::SplayToken`],\n24\t//!   [`crate::hash::HashToken`]).  Every per-collection\n25\t//!   membership is `Option<Token>` on the parent struct; the\n26\t//!   container holds the slot storage.  Zero raw pointers, no\n27\t//!   `unsafe`.\n28\t//! * The C `void* tls_master_ctx`, `void* aead_*`,\n29\t//!   `void* pn_enc/dec`, etc. were external-library handles\n30\t//!   ((picotls, OpenSSL).  Phase 2 replaced them with the\n31\t//!   trait family in [`crate::tls`] (`Session`, `PacketKey`,\n32\t//!   `HeaderKey`, …); backends supply implementations.\n33\t//! * `FILE* F_log` / `FILE* f_binlog` became\n34\t//!   `Option<std::fs::File>` in Phase 1B.\n35\t//! * `struct sockaddr_storage` fields fold into\n36\t//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  Fields that the C code zeros out\n37\t//!   to mean \"address not yet set\" become `Option<SocketAddr>`.\n38\t//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` were\n39\t//!   forward-declared as opaque stubs in\n40\t//!   [`crate`] (the public header).  Their\n41\t//!   real bodies live here; the public module re-exports the\n42\t//!   names so existing `use` paths in other modules keep\n43\t//!   working.\n44\t//! * Function pointer typedefs (`autoqlog_fn`,\n45\t//!   `performance_log_fn`, the spin-bit pair, the\n46\t//!   memlog hook on a connection, `mask_fns_t`) collapse to\n47\t//!   traits per the project rule.  When two function pointers\n48\t//!   are always installed together (`SpinbitDef`,\n49\t//!   `mask_fns_t`) they share one trait.\n50\t//! * Conditional fields gated by `BBRExperiment` and\n51\t//!   `WITH_THREAD_CHECK` are dropped — they are not\n52\t//!   part of the v1 target build.\n53\t//! * The `PARSE_*`/`IS_*_STREAM_ID(_*)` macros that the C\n54\t//!   header inlines as preprocessor macros are translated to\n55\t//!   `pub const fn` helpers.\n56\t\n57\tuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\n58\tuse std::fs::File;\n59\tuse std::path::PathBuf;\n60\t\n61\tuse core::any::Any;\n62\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n63\t\n64\tuse crate::arena::{Arena, Token};\n65\tuse crate::hash::{HashTable, HashToken};\n66\tuse crate::splay::{SplayToken, SplayTree};\n67\tuse crate::{Duration, Instant};\n68\t\n69\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` connection arena.\n70\t///\n71\t/// Phase 4 plan: every C `*mut picoquic_cnx_t` becomes a\n72\t/// [`ConnectionToken`].  Following it requires `quic.connections.get(tok)`\n73\t/// — one indirection through the arena, plus a generation check.\n74\t/// Stable across operations on other connections.\n75\tpub type ConnectionToken = Token<Connection>;\n76\t\n77\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` registered-token replay-protection arena.\n78\tpub type RegisteredTokenToken = Token<RegisteredToken>;\n79\t\n80\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` issued-tickets arena (server-side replay state).\n81\tpub type IssuedTicketToken = Token<IssuedTicket>;\n82\t\n83\t/// Token into the per-`Connection` (or per-`StreamHead`) stream-related\n84\t/// arenas.  Phase 4 may further split these into per-collection types.\n85\tpub type StreamToken = Token<StreamHead>;\n86\tpub type StreamDataToken = Token<StreamDataNode>;\n87\tpub type PacketToken = Token<Packet>;\n88\tpub type SackItemToken = Token<SackItem>;\n89\tpub type LocalConnectionIdToken = Token<LocalConnectionId>;\n90\tpub type PathToken = Token<Path>;\n91\tuse crate::logger::Logger;\n92\tuse crate::{\n93\t    AlpnSelect, CongestionAlgorithm, ConnectionId, ConnectionIdCallback, Fuzz, LossbitVersion,\n94\t    PacketContext, PathStatus, PmtudPolicy, RESET_SECRET_SIZE, SpinbitVersion, State,\n95\t    StreamDataCallback, StreamDirectReceive, TransportParameters,\n96\t};\n97\t\n98\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n99\t// Tunable constants (the `#define`s at the top of the C header).\n100\t\n101\tpub const MAX_PACKET_SIZE: usize = 1536;\n102\tpub const MIN_SEGMENT_SIZE: usize = 256;\n103\tpub const ENFORCED_INITIAL_MTU: usize = 1200;\n104\tpub const ENFORCED_INITIAL_CID_LENGTH: u8 = 8;\n105\tpub const PRACTICAL_MAX_MTU: usize = 1440;\n106\tpub const MIN_STREAM_DATA_FRAGMENT: usize = 512;\n107\tpub const RETRY_SECRET_SIZE: usize = 64;\n108\tpub const RETRY_TOKEN_PAD_SIZE: usize = 26;\n109\tpub const DEFAULT_0RTT_WINDOW: usize = 10 * ENFORCED_INITIAL_MTU;\n110\tpub const NB_PATH_TARGET: usize = 8;\n111\tpub const NB_PATH_DEFAULT: usize = 2;\n112\tpub const MAX_PACKETS_IN_POOL: i32 = 0x2000;\n113\tpub const INITIAL_FLOW_CONTROL_MAX: u64 = 0x100000;\n114\t\n115\tpub const INITIAL_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(250_000);\n116\tpub const TARGET_RENO_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(100_000);\n117\tpub const TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(610_000);\n118\tpub const INITIAL_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(250_000);\n119\tpub const INITIAL_MAX_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000_000);\n120\tpub const LARGE_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(2_000_000);\n121\tpub const MIN_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(50_000);\n122\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000);\n123\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MAX_DEFAULT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(25_000);\n124\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MIN: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000);\n125\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MIN_MAX_VALUE: u64 = 0xFFFFFF;\n126\tpub const RACK_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000);\n127\tpub const MAX_ACK_DELAY_MAX_MS: u64 = 0x4000;\n128\tpub const TOKEN_DELAY_LONG: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(24 * 60 * 60 * 1_000_000);\n129\tpub const TOKEN_DELAY_SHORT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(2 * 60 * 1_000_000);\n130\tpub const CID_REFRESH_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(5 * 1_000_000);\n131\tpub const MTU_LOSS_THRESHOLD: u64 = 10;\n132\t\n133\tpub const BANDWIDTH_ESTIMATE_MAX: u64 = 10_000_000_000;\n134\tpub const BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MIN: u64 = 1000;\n135\tpub const BANDWIDTH_MEDIUM: u64 = 2_000_000;\n136\tpub const MAX_BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MIN: u64 = 1000;\n137\tpub const MAX_BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MAX: u64 = 15000;\n138\t\n139\tpub const MINRTT_MARGIN: u64 = 128;\n140\tpub const MINRTT_THRESHOLD: u64 = 128;\n141\t\n142\tpub const SPURIOUS_RETRANSMIT_DELAY_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000_000);\n143\t\n144\tpub const MICROSEC_SILENCE_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(120_000_000);\n145\tpub const MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(30_000_000);\n146\tpub const MICROSEC_WAIT_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000_000);\n147\t\n148\tpub const MICROSEC_STATELESS_RESET_INTERVAL_DEFAULT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(100_000);\n149\t\n150\tpub const CWIN_INITIAL: u64 = 10 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;\n151\tpub const CWIN_MINIMUM: u64 = 2 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;\n152\t\n153\tpub const DEFAULT_CRYPTO_EPOCH_LENGTH: u64 = 1 << 22;\n154\t\n155\tpub const DEFAULT_SIMULTANEOUS_LOGS: u32 = 32;\n156\tpub const DEFAULT_HALF_OPEN_RETRY_THRESHOLD: u32 = 64;\n157\t\n158\tpub const PN_RANDOM_MIN: u32 = 0xffff;\n159\tpub const PN_RANDOM_RANGE: u32 = 0x10000;\n160\t\n161\tpub const SPIN_RESERVE_MOD_256: u8 = 17;\n162\t\n163\tpub const CHALLENGE_REPEAT_MAX: usize = 3;\n164\t\n165\tpub const ALPN_NUMBER_MAX: usize = 32;\n166\t\n167\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_NEW_RENO: u8 = 1;\n168\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_CUBIC: u8 = 2;\n169\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_DCUBIC: u8 = 3;\n170\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_FAST: u8 = 4;\n171\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_BBR: u8 = 5;\n172\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_PRAGUE: u8 = 6;\n173\tpub const CC_ALGO_NUMBER_BBR1: u8 = 7;\n174\t\n175\tpub const MAX_ACK_RANGE_REPEAT: usize = 4;\n176\tpub const MIN_ACK_RANGE_REPEAT: usize = 2;\n177\t\n178\tpub const DEFAULT_HOLE_PERIOD: u64 = 256;\n179\t\n180\tpub const LOSS_BIT_Q_HALF_PERIOD: u64 = 64;\n181\t\n182\tpub const NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS: usize = 4;\n183\tpub const NUMBER_OF_EPOCH_OFFSETS: usize = NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS + 1;\n184\t\n185\tpub use crate::tp::NB_TP_0RTT;\n186\t\n187\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n188\t// Range / bitfield helper macros.\n189\t\n190\t/// `IN_RANGE(v, min, max)` — true when `min ≤ v ≤ max`\n191\t/// under the C macro's bitfield assumption (`min & max == min`,\n192\t/// `min & bits == 0`, `max & bits == bits`).\n193\t#[inline]\n194\tpub const fn in_range(v: u64, min: u64, max: u64) -> bool {\n195\t    (v & !(min ^ max)) == min\n196\t}\n197\t\n198\t/// `BITS_SET_IN_RANGE(v, min, max, bits)`.\n199\t#[inline]\n200\tpub const fn bits_set_in_range(v: u64, min: u64, max: u64, bits: u64) -> bool {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNJRg8YhsoxF5PXikNyYX1","session_id":"6e30a456-15c0-4e3c-af27-9f4dab375915","uuid":"6c23ccaf-6a12-419b-932a-4138ac86bba8","timestamp":"2026-05-05T21:19:52.220Z"}
