f.congestion_algorithm_id)\n789\t            .field(\n790\t                \"congestion_algorithm_number\",\n791\t                &self.congestion_algorithm_number,\n792\t            )\n793\t            .field(\"ecn_mark\", &self.ecn_mark)\n794\t            .finish_non_exhaustive()\n795\t    }\n796\t}\n797\t\n798\t/// Return the registered congestion-control algorithm table.  In\n799\t/// C this was a pair of `extern` globals\n800\t/// (`congestion_control_algorithms` and\n801\t/// `nb_congestion_control_algorithms`); the Rust API\n802\t/// exposes a single accessor returning a borrowed slice — the\n803\t/// length is implicit.  The slice is empty until\n804\t/// [`register_congestion_control_algorithms`] (or its"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNJRg8YhsoxF5PXikNyYX1","session_id":"6e30a456-15c0-4e3c-af27-9f4dab375915","uuid":"23aa3d68-1ee0-4467-a8e9-99408148ad3c","timestamp":"2026-05-05T21:21:55.260Z"}
