{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0128RUKm1DJeS8Z6em8ta92y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Test cases for `picoquictest/cnx_creation_test.c`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Covers:\n4\t//! * `create_cnx` — builds 7 connections across IPv4 / IPv6 / per-port /\n5\t//!   per-CID combinations, verifies address-based and CID-based lookup,\n6\t//!   iterator count, non-registered lookup, and delete-then-verify.\n7\t//! * `create_quic` — edge cases for QUIC context creation: 0-connection\n8\t//!   clamping, bad cert/key rejection, bad ticket-store tolerance, token-file\n9\t//!   loading, and NULL transport-parameter reset.\n10\t\n11\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n12\t\n13\tuse core::net::{IpAddr, Ipv4Addr, Ipv6Addr, SocketAddr};\n14\t\n15\tuse crate::{ConnectionId, Instant, Quic, RESET_SECRET_SIZE, TransportParameters};\n16\t\n17\t/// Make a fresh `Quic` context with the C test's\n18\t/// `picoquic_create(8, NULL, …)` defaults.  Returns `Option<Box<Quic>>`\n19\t/// directly (the C `NULL` failure goes to `None`).\n20\tfn default_quic() -> Option<Box<Quic>> {\n21\t    Quic::new(\n22\t        8,\n23\t        None,\n24\t        None,\n25\t        None,\n26\t        None,\n27\t        None,\n28\t        None,\n29\t        [0u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n30\t        Instant::from_ticks(0),\n31\t        None,\n32\t        None,\n33\t    )\n34\t}\n35\t\n36\t/// C: `create_cnx_test` in `picoquictest/cnx_creation_test.c`.\n37\t///\n38\t/// Builds 7 connections covering the IPv4 / IPv6 / per-port / per-CID\n39\t/// matrix.  The outer loop runs twice: once with `local_connection_id_length\n40\t/// = 0` (address-based lookup) and once with the default length of 8\n41\t/// (CID-based lookup).  Within each iteration, verifies:\n42\t///\n43\t/// 1. Lookup by address (when no local CID) or by CID (when local CID is\n44\t///    in use) finds every registered connection.\n45\t/// 2. Iterator returns the correct count.\n46\t/// 3. An unregistered address / CID returns `None`.\n47\t/// 4. After deleting even-indexed connections, odd-indexed ones are still\n48\t///    found and even-indexed ones are gone.\n49\t#[test]\n50\tfn create_cnx() {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNJRg8YhsoxF5PXikNyYX1","session_id":"6e30a456-15c0-4e3c-af27-9f4dab375915","uuid":"f268bbc1-d9c4-4f86-bd71-942abfb130ac","timestamp":"2026-05-05T21:28:30.288Z"}
