{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014rbnZLNMMv74X8c4uXKes3","type":"tool_result","content":"1095\t/// Returns `true` when `port` is on the QUIC well-known-port\n1096\t/// blocklist.\n1097\tpub fn check_port_blocked(port: u16) -> bool {\n1098\t    // List is sorted descending; iterate while port <= list[i].\n1099\t    for &blocked in BLOCKED_PORTS {\n1100\t        if port > blocked {\n1101\t            break;\n1102\t        }\n1103\t        if port == blocked {\n1104\t            return true;\n1105\t        }\n1106\t    }\n1107\t    false\n1108\t}\n1109\t\n1110\t/// Returns `true` when `addr_from` belongs to a blocked address\n1111\t/// range.\n1112\tpub fn check_addr_blocked(addr_from: &SocketAddr) -> bool {\n1113\t    check_port_blocked(addr_from.port())\n1114\t}\n1115\t\n1116\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1117\t// QUIC context: construction, TLS configuration, default policies.\n1118\t//\n1119\t// `picoquic_create` is the canonical constructor in the C source;\n1120\t// here it is `Quic::new`.  The setters that follow are all on the\n1121\t// QUIC context; per-connection siblings live in `impl Connection` further\n1122\t// down.\n1123\t\n1124\timpl Quic {\n1125\t    /// Build a QUIC context with the supplied certificate paths,\n1126\t    /// default callbacks, and reset seed.\n1127\t    ///\n1128\t    /// Pointer-shape choices, derived from `quic/quicctx.c:634` and\n1129\t    /// `quic/sockloop.c:2009`:\n1130\t    ///\n1131\t    /// * Every `char const*` parameter is `Option<&str>` (the C\n1132\t    ///   source passes `NULL` to mean \"absent\").\n1133\t    /// * `default_callback_fn` + `default_callback_ctx` collapse to\n1134\t    ///   one `Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>`.\n1135\t    /// * `connection_id_callback` + `connection_id_callback_data` collapse to\n1136\t    ///   `Option<Box<dyn ConnectionIdCallback>>`.\n1137\t    /// * `reset_seed[16]` is `[u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE]` taken by\n1138\t    ///   value (the C body deep-copies it into the context).\n1139\t    /// * `ticket_encryption_key` + `ticket_encryption_key_length`\n1140\t    ///   collapse to a borrowed `Option<&[u8]>`.\n1141\t    /// * The C `p_simulated_time: uint64_t*` parameter is dropped\n1142\t    ///   — the test simulator owns its own clock and threads the\n1143\t    ///   value through `current_time` directly.\n1144\t    ///\n1145\t    /// Returns `None` when context creation fails (the C side\n1146\t    /// returned `NULL`).\n1147\t    #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n1148\t    pub fn new(\n1149\t        _max_nb_connections: u32,\n1150\t        _cert_file_name: Option<&str>,\n1151\t        _key_file_name: Option<&str>,\n1152\t        _cert_root_file_name: Option<&str>,\n1153\t        _default_alpn: Option<&str>,\n1154\t        _default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n1155\t        _cnx_id_callback: Option<Box<dyn ConnectionIdCallback>>,\n1156\t        _reset_seed: [u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n1157\t        _current_time: Instant,\n1158\t        _ticket_file_name: Option<&str>,\n1159\t        _ticket_encryption_key: Option<&[u8]>,\n1160\t    ) -> Option<Box<Quic>> {\n1161\t        todo!()\n1162\t    }\n1163\t\n1164\t    // The C `picoquic_free` entry point is dropped from the Rust API\n1165\t    // — context cleanup is the job of `Drop`, which Phase 3 will\n1166\t    // implement.\n1167\t\n1168\t    /// Toggle low-memory mode (smaller buffers, more aggressive\n1169\t    /// reclaim)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNJRg8YhsoxF5PXikNyYX1","session_id":"6e30a456-15c0-4e3c-af27-9f4dab375915","uuid":"5b6d86ee-bf59-48e9-830f-7afb23f4e277","timestamp":"2026-05-05T21:31:24.502Z"}
