{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01DUJqtWc9kKY6gKQ1Zfzfed","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The phase4_check script is reporting failures, but those are in comment references to `todo!()`, not actual code. The script's regex `r\"\\btodo!\\s*\\(\"` doesn't distinguish between code and comments. This is a false positive issue with the script.\n\nThe actual code has no `todo!()` bodies left. But the requirement says \"All four must succeed\" - including the phase4_check script. So I need to either:\n1. Fix the phase4_check.py script to ignore comments\n2. Update the doc comments in lib.rs and internal.rs to remove the `todo!()` references\n\nSince the task says \"No edits outside `rs/fq/src/`\" and the check script is in `scripts/`, I should update the doc comments in the Rust files to remove the `todo!()` string references.\n\n\nLooking more carefully at what the script is actually detecting - it's finding `todo!()` references in comments near the `close_immediate` and `val64` functions, not in the function bodies themselves, since both of those have complete implementations. The script's `fn_at` function is picking up these comment references when it shouldn't be. the todo!() at line 102. The `fn_at` function searches backwards from a given position to find the most recent function declaration, so for a todo!() at line 1881 in a comment about `close_immediate`, it would locate that function itself as the most recent one before that position. Similarly, for a todo!() at line 477 in a comment about `current_time`, it would find whichever function was most recently declared before that line.\n\nThis means the phase4_check script is reporting these as failures because it's attributing the todo!() markers to the wrong functions—they're actually in doc comments or comments within function bodies, not in the function code itself. I could fix this by removing the todo!() references from the comments, since updating the check script itself isn't really an option here.\n\nThe cleanest approach is to reword the doc comments to avoid literal `todo!()` mentions—replacing them with descriptions like \"stub\" or \"stub bodies\" instead. I need to go through and update these references in both the main file and internal.rs so the phase4_check passes. I can edit scripts/phase4_check.py since it's in the allowed directories, but updating the stale doc comments in the Rust files is simpler—there are only 5 occurrences and they're outdated anyway since Phase 4 has already filled in the implementations. I'll fix those comments to reflect the current state.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1464,"cache_read_input_tokens":60991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1464},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e30a456-15c0-4e3c-af27-9f4dab375915","uuid":"e794c00f-a6cb-4006-96bb-b94a9149bca7"}
